      "body": "I have the same error as above, where I've exported 'PORT=7575' as an environment variable. I'm not sure if my configuration (running podman but not exposing its socket) diverges too much from what you're expecting:\n\n`sudo podman run -d --name homarr --user 1000:1000 -e 'PORT=7575' -p 7575:7575 -e 'SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY=82bf9755b947c26f59717f2d16e6630278262dc1805399a130162537ec074077' --mount type=bind,source=/home/namgo/homarr-mountpoint,destination=/appdata,bind-propagation=rslave ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr:latest`\n\n to add some logs to the above error as encountered in my own configuration:\n`curl localhost:7575`\ngives a 500 http error and in logs:\n```\nError [TRPCClientError]: fetch failed\n    at ta.from (.next/server/src/middleware.js:16:1640)\n    at <unknown> (.next/server/src/middleware.js:16:34612) {\n  shape: undefined,\n  data: undefined,\n  meta: undefined,\n  [cause]: TypeError: fetch failed\n      at tw (.next/server/src/middleware.js:16:5661)\n      at async tb (.next/server/src/middleware.js:16:5763) {\n    [cause]: Error: connect ECONNREFUSED 10.88.0.13:3000\n        at <unknown> (Error: connect ECONNREFUSED 10.88.0.13:3000) {\n      errno: -111,\n      code: 'ECONNREFUSED',\n      syscall: 'connect',\n      address: '10.88.0.13',\n      port: 3000\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen a port is unspecified in the latest homarr container, it appears to default to `:3000`, is that correct?\n\nWhen run with `-p 3000:3000` and no `PORT` environment variable specified, I am able to connect on `http://localhost:3000`. 7575/tcp doesn't appear to be in use in the container when running `podman exec [container] netstat `\n\n",
